WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:12.360
North Korea is located in Northeast Asia.
It is a socialist system.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:17.580
It was established on a Soviet model.
The economy is centrally controlled.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:25.480
That system worked well in the early 60s but it ran into roadblocks, in part because of North Korea's isolation.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:34.160
China is a kind of lifeline for goods, energy, and food to
North Korea, and North Korea is reported

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:40.060
to have as much as one quarter of its GDP
devoted to the military.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:43.680
North Korea is estimated to have enough material

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.660
to build 10 to 16 nuclear weapons in 2016.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:54.500
They've also been trying to develop a nuclear bomb
small enough that it could fit onto a missile--

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:59.620
in other words they're trying to expand their ability
to deliver a nuclear weapon

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:05.500
to a neighboring country, or, in the long term,
possibly even to the United States.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:14.080
The U.S.-North Korea relationship may be
the most enduring hostile relationship

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.900
the United States has had with any country in the world.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:22.760
Arguably the origins of the nuclear program in
North Korea go back to the 1960s.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:29.600
It didn't really become of concern on the part of the U.S. until the late 1980s, at which time

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:36.040
a nuclear reactor was detected by satellites.
The U.S. began to focus on what could be done

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:40.480
in order to stop North Korea
from pursuing further nuclear development.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.460
One method has been to 
negotiate with North Korea.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:50.740
Subsequently, the United States has used sanctions
following North Korea's nuclear tests.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:58.000
Another important priority of U.S. policy toward
North Korea has been deterrence.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:07.380
The main concern that the United States
has related to North Korea is in maintaining

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.580
the stability of South Korea and
preventing a war on the Korean Peninsula

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.860
that could evolve into a regional conflict.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:18.380
Since the end of the Korean War,
the United States has maintained troops

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:24.000
in South Korea, and the U.S. interest in the 
peninsula is directly related to its

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.220
security commitments to South Korea. In addition
the U.S. has an alliance with Japan.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:33.320
Another U.S. interest is the fact that
the North Korean regime is probably

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.400
the worst human rights violator in the world.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.780
China is the country that North Korea
is most dependent on, but its views

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:45.360
about the desired end state on the Korean Peninsula are different from those of the United States

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.040
and South Korea.
One policy option for the United States

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.180
in confronting the challenge posed by
North Korea's nuclear development might be

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.840
to manage the problem.
The U.S. could try to slow down

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:02.280
the North Korean nuclear program through
isolation, through sanctions. The U.S. could

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:07.340
continue to pursue deterrence, and they
can try to put pressure on North Korea

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.780
to get the North Koreans to move
in a different direction.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:13.500
A second policy option would be to
go back to the negotiating table.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.380
Another policy option might be
a preventive strike against

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.320
North Korea's nuclear program.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:25.320
There's really no direct means that
the United States and North Korea have

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.200
to address their differences that does not

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:32.700
ultimately involve North Korea's neighbors
and American allies.

